WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.640
Everything in life
is a negotiation.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.060
When you cross the
street is a negotiation.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.120
Getting your coffee at
Starbucks is a negotiation.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.120
You're probably in three
to seven negotiations

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.350
every single day.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.620
Your life could be in a
completely different place

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.420
just by improving
how you negotiate.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.650
REPORTER: Negotiators are
working around the clock.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.650
REPORTER: The deadline
for execution has passed.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.108
REPORTER: With us now to help
break down the investigation,

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:28.500
FBI special agent, hostage
negotiator Christopher Voss.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.400
My role as a hostage negotiator
was to connect authentically

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.620
with the victim,
the victim's family,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.450
and with the hostage taker.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.300
Everybody really
deserves to have somebody

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.770
hear what they have to say.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.290
In my MasterClass, I'm going
to give you all the strategies

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.800
and tactics that I developed
as one of the top hostage

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.360
negotiators in the world.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.610
You're going to learn
everything from bargaining

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.520
to reading body language
to the neuroscience

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.955
that you can use to literally
bend people's reality.

00:00:59.955 --> 00:01:03.330
You know, negotiation is letting
the other side have your way.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.270
So mirroring creates
the opportunity for them

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.340
actually to present
you with your deal,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.200
only they thought
it was their idea.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.160
It's just the simple repetition
of the last one to three words

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.410
of what somebody said.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.240
We've got the actual recording
on the Chase Manhattan Bank

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.565
robbery hostage taking.

00:01:19.565 --> 00:01:20.880
CHRIS VOSS: (RECORDING)
We've got a van out here.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.720
Know anything about it?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.920
BANK ROBBER: (RECORDING) You
guys chased my driver away.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.650
CHRIS VOSS: (RECORDING) We
chased your driver away?

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.750
My training was to mirror,
and the bank robber

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.350
started blurting out stuff that
he had no intention of saying.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.680
People love to be mirrored.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.470
They love to be
encouraged to go on.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.950
These skills help you
improve your life.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.630
Sometimes people say
to me, these tools

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:45.710
are just manipulation.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.380
It's about win/lose.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.740
That is not the case.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.138
Great negotiation is
about great collaboration.

00:01:52.138 --> 00:01:54.305
Why does it matter to you
that you should get better

00:01:54.305 --> 00:01:55.460
at negotiation?

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.630
Because however your life
is now, you can do better.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:04.840
I'm Chris Voss, and
this is my MasterClass.

